  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A sphere of density <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\rho\"></span> and radius <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"R\"></span> rests on the bottom of a tank of water. The buoyancy force on the sphere is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F_{1}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>A sphere of density <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2\\rho\"></span> and radius <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{R}{2}\"></span> is at the bottom of the same tank. The buoyancy force on the second sphere is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F_{2}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>What is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{F_{1}}{F_{2}}\"></span>?</p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\">2</li><li data-label=\"B\">4</li><li data-label=\"C\">8</li><li data-label=\"D\">16</li></ol>"
